2. Permitted Use

You may use, modify, and distribute this Software for personal projects and
non-commercial business ventures that do not generate revenue in any form.

You may build upon this Software for personal or non-commercial use, provided
that you do not violate the restrictions outlined in Section 3.

You may distribute physical copies or hardware containing this Software,
provided that the amount charged does not exceed the exact documented cost of
physical materials and/or shipping. Any amount charged must be equal to or
less than the actual out-of-pocket cost incurred. Charging even one cent
above the documented cost of materials and/or shipping constitutes a
commercial transaction and is prohibited without explicit written permission
from the original authors. Operating at a loss is permitted.

3. License Versioning and Mandatory Upgrades

  a. Current and Future Versions

     This license may be revised and updated by Raymond Newman at any time.
     Each new version will be assigned a unique version number and
     publication date and will be made publicly available via the official
     Ray's Tech Services communication channels or repository. All versions
     of this license are authored solely by Raymond Newman or under his
     explicit direction.

  b. Mandatory Upgrade Obligation

     Any individual, entity, or project using, distributing, or building
     upon Software governed by any version of this license must upgrade to
     the most current published version of the RTSSL within seven (7)
     calendar days of that version's public release date.

     Failure to upgrade within this period constitutes a violation of this
     license and will result in immediate revocation of all rights granted
     herein until compliance is achieved.

     "Upgrading" means replacing the license file in the Software's
     repository or distribution with the new version and ensuring all
     documentation, notices, and references reflect the updated version
     number.

  c. Contributor Agreement — Automatic License Migration

     By submitting any contribution to Software governed by this license —
     including but not limited to code, documentation, assets, bug fixes,
     translations, or any other material — each contributor irrevocably
     agrees that:

       - Their contributions are provided under the current version of the
         RTSSL at the time of submission, AND
       - Their contributions will automatically and immediately fall under
         any future version of the RTSSL upon that version's public
         release, without requiring any further action, consent, or
         notification from the contributor.
       - No contributor may restrict, withdraw, or place additional
         conditions on their contributions in response to a new version
         of this license.
       - This agreement is binding on all past, present, and future
         contributions to any Software under this license, from the
         moment of first contribution.

     Contributors who do not agree to these terms must not submit
     contributions to Software governed by this license.

  d. No Version Pinning

     You may not pin, lock, or otherwise restrict Software governed by
     this license to an older version of the RTSSL. Distributing,
     deploying, or publishing Software under any version of the RTSSL
     other than the most current published version — beyond the seven
     (7) day grace period — is a violation of this license.

4. Business Use

  a. Small Business Use (Fewer than 100 Employees)

     Any business, organization, or entity with a total headcount of fewer
     than 100 employees — including full-time, part-time, contract, and
     any other compensated workers — may use this Software at no charge,
     subject to all other terms and restrictions of this license. The
     prohibition on selling, monetizing, or profiting from the Software
     remains fully in effect regardless of business size.

     Employee count is determined at the time of deployment and must be
     re-evaluated at each anniversary of first use. If at any point the
     organization's headcount meets or exceeds 100 employees, the
     organization must immediately come into compliance with Section 4(b).

  b. Large Business Use (100 or More Employees)

     Any business, organization, or entity with a total headcount of 100
     or more employees must pay a licensing fee to Ray's Tech Services
     as a condition of use. The fee is calculated as follows:

       - $0.10 USD (ten cents) per device on which the Software is
         installed or running, OR
       - $0.10 USD (ten cents) per user who accesses or interacts with
         the Software in any capacity,

     whichever of the two figures is higher. Both counts must be assessed
     honestly and in good faith, and must be re-evaluated and paid on an
     annual basis from the date of first deployment.

     Payment must be made exclusively in Bitcoin (BTC) at the current
     market equivalent of the calculated USD fee at the time of payment.
     Payment must be directed to Ray's Tech Services via the contact
     information provided in Section 12. Proof of payment must be retained
     by the paying organization and made available to Raymond Newman upon
     request.
     Payment is due on the first (1st) day of each calendar month, based
     on the device and user counts assessed at that time. Failure to submit
     payment by the first of the month constitutes a violation of this license
     and will result in immediate revocation of all rights granted herein until
     payment is received and confirmed.

     All network transaction fees, including but not limited to Bitcoin network
     fees and any associated transfer costs, are the sole responsibility of the
     paying organization and must be covered in full such that Ray's Tech Services
     receives the exact calculated USD-equivalent amount in Bitcoin with no deductions.
     Underpayment due to network fees does not constitute valid payment.

     Use of the Software by an organization subject to this section without
     payment constitutes a violation of this license and will result in
     immediate revocation of all rights granted herein.

  c. Headcount Calculation

     For the purposes of this license, employee headcount includes all
     individuals who perform work for the organization in exchange for any
     form of compensation, including but not limited to salary, hourly
     wages, equity, or contract payments. Volunteers, unpaid interns, and
     non-compensated contributors are excluded from headcount calculation.
     Parent companies, subsidiaries, and affiliated entities are each
     evaluated independently unless they share unified IT infrastructure,
     in which case the combined headcount applies.

5. Restricted Use

You may not use this Software for any commercial purpose, including but not
limited to:

  - Selling, licensing, or otherwise monetizing the Software.
  - Using the Software as part of a product, service, or business that
    generates revenue.
  - Using the Software in any company, organization, or personal project that
    is intended to generate revenue, either directly or indirectly.
  - Charging any amount above the exact documented cost of physical materials
    and/or shipping when distributing physical copies or hardware containing
    this Software.

These restrictions apply regardless of business size. Payment of the fee
described in Section 4(b) grants the right to use the Software within the
organization but does not grant any right to sell, sublicense, or monetize
the Software itself.

If your use case involves monetization or exceeds the cost-recovery
distribution terms outlined in Section 2, you must obtain explicit written
permission from the original authors of the Software.

