7. Network Copyleft — Software as a Service

The copyleft obligations defined in Section 6 are explicitly triggered by
network use. If you modify this Software, or incorporate it into a larger
work, and make that work available to any third party over a network —
including but not limited to web applications, APIs, SaaS platforms,
hosted services, or any other form of remote access — the following
conditions apply:

  - You must make the complete corresponding source code of the modified
    or combined work available to all users interacting with it over the
    network, at no charge.
  - This source code must be provided under the terms of this license
    (RTSSL) and must be made available via a prominent and accessible
    means, such as a public repository link or an in-application notice.
  - The act of running modified Software on a server and allowing third
    parties to interact with it constitutes distribution under this
    license, regardless of whether any files are transferred to the
    end user.
  - This provision applies even if the Software is used internally within
    an organization and accessed by members of that organization over
    a network.

